The chronicles of Famrer the Archelogist : Chapter One

Famrer the Archelogist started down the long, winding stairway into the
Dungeons of Nethack.  He felt a foreboding feeling, but since the moon
was full he thought nothing of it.  In the first level he finds the one
thing that will make life very hard for him:  A cursed -2 Orcish Helm!

Very angry, and also glad for the Acid Blob corpse that he found (in case
he finds a Cocatrice laying around) he journeys to the second level, now
being at level 3...  First thing he sees:  A chest (oval keyhole)...kick
it?  Nope, hurt myself.  Force it? POP and it's open.  He finds an uncursed
+0 pair of Fencing Gloves and is greatly pleased to discover that they are
really Gauntlets of Power!  He also finds a Potion of Detect Object, a 
Spellbook of Levitation, and a Spellbook of Remove Curse - and goes up to
level 4!  Decending again...

He finds a fountain (in the Oracles room, natch) and dips the -2 helm in 
it to uncurse it...First try - nothing.  Second try - it becomes Uncursed.
Quaff to ease my hunger - Just before it dries up, 'You have released a 
water demon! -more-' O boy.  Just what a poor 4th level guy needs.  'greatful
for his release, he grands you a wish! -more-'  Wonderful!  So, wish for
'Blessed +3 Gray Dragon Scale Mail' and get a Blessed GDSM...good!  Now,
getting rid of the helm, I put on all of my things and walk on.  Finding a
Moonstone Ring, I put it on...the Black dragon that just entered the room
turns into a Chamelion - 'ring of protection from shape-shifters' is nice!

Going down another level (after getting stuff, etc.) I find a shop...I 
purchase the Identify scrolls that are in there for 98 each - read one to
identify the wire ring I picked up somewhere - +1 ring of Protection!  I
continue - this isn't such a bad game after all!  I even dispatched Lerka's
Ghost on the 4th level!  No sweat.  More mediocre playing...now have 2 +2
bullwhips, +1 fedora, +4 GDSM (thanks to 2 scrolls of Enchant armor - 
one blessed) and 2 +2 bullwhips...with my 25 str. then I do 9-11 damage!
not bad!  And my armor class is currently -12...

'You feel you were here in a prevoius lifetime.'  So, here's the Rogue level,
with Michael Toy's ghost standing next to me!  Beat the heck out of him,
get 5 food rations and a 'Blessed +1 ring of regeneration' from that level!

Going down I really need the ring of prot. and the ring of regen - I run into
a Throne Room between me and the exit stairs!  I sit on the throne and get
no wishes...rats...

So, it is now time for supper and I regretfully save the game...backing up 
the save file just in case.  Funny, I never knew that the game would say
'Your score blew the others away!' if you get more than 2x the 1st place...

